{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfURMmXEnP5z8MSYVfk7k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 04 is solved and written up. Nine items remain unchecked, so no LOOP_COMPLETE line.\n\n**What was built.** The two changes of the 2026-09-26 `better_move` fix are now separately revertable behind flags that default off: a new C entry point `cs_decide_variant` with variant bits, wired through `decide_native` and `decide` as `old_close_count`, `old_rule_order` and `subset_after_better_move`. The old entry points keep their signatures. The default path is byte-identical to the previous library on 10,248 calls. `learning/fix_cost.py` runs the four variants (plus one candidate) through the differential harness at n ≤ 40 and pairs refutation nodes at 41–100.\n\n**Reproduction.** The pre-fix variant reproduces every recorded pre-fix number exactly: §15's 56 instances / 88 false answers, the bug report's node totals, `Random-100-100-2-4_0` at 93,127,027 nodes in 38.8 s, and the recorded `nodes_csearch` in both campaign files.\n\n**Findings** (`reports/ml_nature.md` §31, tables in `reports/fix_cost_tables.md`):\n- Both changes are necessary for soundness. Reverting the close count alone gives 1 false refutation at n ≤ 40, reverting the rule order alone gives 36, both together 56. No revert is a candidate.\n- At n ≤ 40 the reordering carries the cost: 81% of the log-cost, 6.4% of total nodes, against 1.1% for the close count.\n- At 41–100 the fix costs 1.54× nodes and 1.30× seconds. The reordering still dominates total nodes (1.48 against 1.06), but per instance the two are comparable, and the close count is the larger on half-ratio and SCOOP instances. The ridge instance splits as 2.26× close, ≥ 8.7× order.\n- One correction to the bug report: the 10 × 13 minimal instance needs both bugs, not the cycle alone.\n- A fifth, non-revert composition (`bm-first`: better move first, subset rule barred from citing what it discarded) is sound on every call measured, 2% dearer at n ≤ 40, 15% cheaper in nodes at 41–100, and even in seconds because it is slower per node.\n\n**Recommendation, stated and not applied.** Keep today's rule. `bm-first` is worth tuning and re-timing on the 125 × 125 density-2/4 classes before any decision.\n\n**Bookkeeping.** Full suite 1,138 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed in 86 s after the last edit. `tests/test_fix_cost.py` adds 8 tests. PROGRESS.md has the iteration entry with the note that the literal \"flag never changes a status\" criterion cannot hold for deliberate reverts, and what the tests assert instead. `iterations.md` marks 04 done. Nothing written to `solutions/`; recertify untouched; nothing committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":251869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":548,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":773,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c519ced9-8245-4cc5-ac30-cc8ecb8c61ca","uuid":"3c63134a-69f2-4e91-b51f-cd490950178d","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:31:09.374Z","request_id":"req_011CfURMhvCjWnYVfgGRUkwg"}
